        <headline>Special Weather Statement issued September 25 at 4:32PM AST by NWS San Juan PR</headline>
        <description>At 432 PM AST, Doppler radar was tracking a strong thunderstorm over
Utuado, moving west at 10 mph.

HAZARD...Wind gusts up to 50 mph. Funnel clouds or brief weak
tornadoes are possible.

SOURCE...Radar indicated.

IMPACT...Gusty winds could knock down tree limbs and blow around
unsecured objects.

Locations impacted include...
Utuado, Rafael Capo, Cayuco and Quebrada.
</description>
        <instruction>Monitor the weather situation closely and be alert for threatening
weather conditions.</instruction>
